===Genera===
The genera included in the tribe {{as of|2023|January|lc=yes}} are as follows,<ref name=CalvZappForeLohm11/> with species counts based on [[Plants of the World Online]]:
* ''[[Hatiora]]'' <small>[[Nathaniel Lord Britton|Britton]] & [[Joseph Nelson Rose|Rose]]</small> – 3 species;<ref name=POWO_5359-1>{{citation |title=''Hatiora'' Britton & Rose |work=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew|url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:5359-1 |access-date=2023-01-24 }}</ref> synonyms include ''Epiphyllopsis'', ''Hariota'' <small>DC non Andan.</small>, ''Pseudozygocactus''; it has been included in ''Rhipsalis''<ref name=Ande2001p375-7/>
* ''[[Lepismium]]'' <small>[[Ludwig Karl Georg Pfeiffer|Pfeiff.]]</small> – 7 species;<ref name=POWO_30004247-2>{{citation |title=''Lepismium'' Pfeiff. |work=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew|url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:30004247-2 |access-date=2023-01-24 }}</ref> synonyms include ''Acanthorhipsalis'', ''Lymanbensonia'', ''Pfeiffera''; it has been included in ''Rhipsalis''<ref>{{Harvnb|Anderson|2001|pp=386–391}}</ref>
* ''[[Rhipsalidopsis]]'' <small>Britton & Rose</small> – 2 species<ref name=POWO_77198976-1>{{citation |title=''Rhipsalidopsis'' Britton & Rose |work=[[Plants of the World Online]] |publisher=[[Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew]] |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:77198976-1 |access-date=2023-01-24}}</ref> (plus an artificial hybrid); included in ''Schlumbergera'' by Calvente et al. (2011)
* ''[[Rhipsalis]]'' <small>[[Joseph Gaertner|Gaertn.]]</small> – 45 species;<ref name=POWO_331903-2>{{citation |title=''Rhipsalis'' Gaertn. |work=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew|url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:331903-2 |access-date=2023-01-24 }}</ref> synonyms include ''Erythrorhipsalis'';<ref>{{Harvnb|Anderson|2001|p=612}}</ref> most species in the tribe have been placed here at one time or another
* ''[[Schlumbergera]]'' <small>[[Charles Antoine Lemaire|Lem.]]</small> – 7 species;<ref name=POWO_5529-1>{{citation |title=''Schlumbergera'' Lem. |work=Plants of the World Online |publisher=Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew|url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:5529-1 |access-date=2023-01-24 }}</ref> synonyms include ''Epiphyllanthus'', ''Epiphyllum'' <small>Pfeiffer non. Haworth</small> and ''Zygocactus''<ref>{{Harvnb|Anderson|2001|p=623}}</ref>

